.TH WELLSENSORS 1 "August 2026" "wellsensors 1.2" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
Wellsensors \- R e a d s   t h e r m a l   a n d   f a n   s e n s o r s   f r o m   h w m o n   v i a   l m _ s e n s o r s   w h e n
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellsensors
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellsensors
.PP
Reads thermal and fan sensors from hwmon via lm_sensors when
present, and shows a live temperature overview including GPU sensors
through nvidia-smi when available.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1)
